#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124142 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f232aed9-1584-5e57-a881-226a6876384a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/id #uuid "001af492-25b1-5f75-b030-668708eee118" :question/math-academy-id "e-15602" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations: \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041770/assets/a664a3af1ba466491d209dadd32a3be026a5179ac2d0281b55f30917f9ab016b.png)\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?" :question/worked-solution "These parametric equations are equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2+2t \\\\ 5t \\\\ 1-t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2t \\\\ 5t \\\\ -t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124143 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3699391-68e8-5c59-8ca2-83fded9f22de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Parallel To a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/id #uuid "7a6038c2-3f7b-5dfa-a9e2-256b246fcc20" :question/math-academy-id "e-15603" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041770/assets/a4c6f7b2422f1515e1708bf1641dcbec57eeb2d85e4ac03bd98668db34088afc.png)\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5-t \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-t \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nThis implies that the line passes through the point $(5,3,1)$ and is parallel to the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041770/assets/11701a2d63851a3f241d8bd905693abaaa6eda6fe4ba0c5710c92d8189595ffd.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124144 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "debd4ccc-de40-55a6-9236-9bf9fff0bdb1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Line"}] :question/id #uuid "173b99e8-d00c-57c8-995e-ba198361480e" :question/math-academy-id "e-15604" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the line shown in the figure below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041770/assets/53386f04f4025fda6ab579113a8ecb53a19f4dc0a77903adc05bac3a71429717.png)" :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(3,3,-5)$ and $Q(1,0,-1)$. Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2t \\\\ -3t \\\\ 4t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3-2t \\\\ 3-3t \\\\ -5+4t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3-2t \\\\ y=3-3t \\\\ z=-5+4t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124145 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d275a218-aa12-54bd-a4ff-4be892226f4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Segment"}] :question/id #uuid "a9c13555-9d30-5dfc-be5a-13f0597c2ada" :question/math-academy-id "e-15605" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overline{PQ},$ where $P(1,-5,3)$ and $Q(0, 4, -4).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-t \\\\ 9t \\\\ -7t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1-t \\\\ -5+9t \\\\ 3-7t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t \\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overline{PQ}$ are the following:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041770/assets/63d8bf337e8d7fa2323eb049b51d40349564336a12d53ffd3259b1e7211ef7dd.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314759 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3699391-68e8-5c59-8ca2-83fded9f22de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Parallel To a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d313486-e349-59a2-b8d5-02e13fbf6d36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314761} {:answer/id #uuid "6eab4365-8239-52a0-a5f3-dd30891fced6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314762} {:answer/id #uuid "e97f4fd1-8bdf-5b77-8a43-223fd5730ee5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314763} {:answer/id #uuid "1e232130-0aa4-523d-ad8b-da996a44179d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314764} {:answer/id #uuid "a27c9435-0f0a-5c61-a3d5-13481412c664" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d313486-e349-59a2-b8d5-02e13fbf6d36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314761} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8e2521f-de41-5643-ba87-56daab4b42c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314760}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "11bd8602-a2be-5ae4-8ba8-6a2ffe62757c" :question/math-academy-id "q-127043" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{1}{3}t-2 \\\\ y=5-4t \\\\ z=2t+\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}t-2 \\\\ 5-4t \\\\ 2t+\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}t \\\\ -4t \\\\ 2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(-2,5,\\frac{1}{7})$  and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "debd4ccc-de40-55a6-9236-9bf9fff0bdb1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87c2d36b-627d-5f64-8a6c-a09f1ad9c528" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=7-3t \\\\ y=-11+2t \\\\ z=3+7t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314789} {:answer/id #uuid "6753ca76-c745-5e12-977d-db60884dea68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=7+3t \\\\ y=-11+2t \\\\ z=3-7t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314790} {:answer/id #uuid "b42ef42e-1337-5b35-ba54-883e7d684a97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=7-3t \\\\ y=-11-2t \\\\ z=4+7t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314791} {:answer/id #uuid "00448bb0-44e2-58c8-92b1-aeda5e4b0a22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=7+3t \\\\ y=11+2t \\\\ z=3-7t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314792} {:answer/id #uuid "d5bdabce-6dcf-5334-a2f9-c1909f66c74a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=7+3t \\\\ y=11-2t \\\\ z=3+7t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87c2d36b-627d-5f64-8a6c-a09f1ad9c528" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=7-3t \\\\ y=-11+2t \\\\ z=3+7t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314789} :answer-field/id #uuid "65f4f4c5-0296-597d-bba7-0781ac08f9b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314788}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d58634d7-9f45-5d26-80b4-6e2ac3418e11" :question/math-academy-id "q-127065" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the straight line that passes through $P(7,-11,3)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨-3,2,7⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, the vector equation of the line is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3t \\\\ 2t \\\\ 7t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7-3t \\\\ -11+2t \\\\ 3+7t\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Therefore, the parametric equations are:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=7-3t \\\\ y=-11+2t \\\\ z=3+7t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314807 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3699391-68e8-5c59-8ca2-83fded9f22de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Parallel To a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "329c241f-0d93-5f7f-8960-fd8b6d634cf1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314809} {:answer/id #uuid "156453ff-6483-5567-8cba-b2845dd6a48d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314810} {:answer/id #uuid "e29dbda6-f364-588c-9e00-f11da1bf3f40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314811} {:answer/id #uuid "5b12767e-c18b-54c4-a4ba-cb0bacd89255" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314812} {:answer/id #uuid "8b2472f9-1cff-5da2-877c-22cf92446010" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e29dbda6-f364-588c-9e00-f11da1bf3f40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314811} :answer-field/id #uuid "d429ff55-de2b-5d12-a616-8527bdc051ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314808}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ff24dde6-0a9a-5793-9f5c-5477e633ad31" :question/math-academy-id "q-22301" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+3t \\\\ y=2-4t \\\\ z=2+t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1+3t \\\\ 2-4t \\\\ 2+t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ -4t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nThis implies that the line passes through the point $(1,2,2)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314828 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d275a218-aa12-54bd-a4ff-4be892226f4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0987641c-7f73-5003-941d-7fe503310468" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4+4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0987641c-7f73-5003-941d-7fe503310468" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4+4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314830} :answer-field/id #uuid "a18e49a9-1921-5eab-b6c4-24acf04b56ee" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314829} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "816b6bec-0b6a-5b61-9553-99760ba5cd46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "816b6bec-0b6a-5b61-9553-99760ba5cd46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314832} :answer-field/id #uuid "2280d646-8b5f-5bb4-a129-7d8436245450" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314831} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b0ad7a4-e070-58df-b6bb-ed9592dd31cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b0ad7a4-e070-58df-b6bb-ed9592dd31cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314834} :answer-field/id #uuid "7481a238-1235-5bf9-ba0f-01c8cc89f42e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314833}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c29e7b23-e914-5d7e-8ead-87a0c88d3626" :question/math-academy-id "q-236982" :question/problem "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(-4,-2,4)$ and $Q(0,8,3).$\n\n| $x=$ | {{field-1}} | $t\\in [$ {{field-2}} $,1]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y=$ | $-2+10t$ |  |\n| $z=$ | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4t \\\\ 10t \\\\ -t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4+4t \\\\ -2+10t \\\\ 4-t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t\\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-4+4t \\\\ y=-2+10t \\\\ z=4-t\\end{aligned}\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314841 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d275a218-aa12-54bd-a4ff-4be892226f4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62a025e7-22f9-55a7-bbec-9097a8473a91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314843} {:answer/id #uuid "1aace4d2-f6bb-5a1c-932a-7999444d7f8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62a025e7-22f9-55a7-bbec-9097a8473a91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314843} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac00e134-fb5e-53b9-991c-6c847a1416c5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74e7409c-22e7-5d40-a6de-ccaadd3efcd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74e7409c-22e7-5d40-a6de-ccaadd3efcd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314846} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3c61ccd-cd26-564a-99e4-21625f8441de" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314845}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8cbe2a7-0a06-5ac6-9b88-c4bca06e5838" :question/math-academy-id "q-236991" :question/problem "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(2,1,0)$ and $Q(3,2,-1).$\n\n| $x=$ | $2+t$ | $t\\in [$ {{field-1}} $,1]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y=$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| $z=$ | $-t$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ t \\\\ -t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2+t \\\\ 1+t \\\\ -t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t\\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2+t \\\\ y=1+t \\\\ z=-t\\end{aligned}\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314847 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3699391-68e8-5c59-8ca2-83fded9f22de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Parallel To a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67cfb500-43a2-5211-8e9a-e3faebd7b5a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314849} {:answer/id #uuid "0aeabd2b-6e76-586a-be05-d60c99344de0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314850} {:answer/id #uuid "cf939b94-ee78-5c4e-84c4-ba0ecd81fc34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314851} {:answer/id #uuid "2b610f73-4981-5b93-8f36-423dd2860458" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314852} {:answer/id #uuid "a66a1959-ab87-514d-9718-97791864a033" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314853}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a66a1959-ab87-514d-9718-97791864a033" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314853} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a9de36f-432b-5923-a955-e804f64b9e69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314848}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "276a7616-1504-50b7-889c-ca5f9580b20b" :question/math-academy-id "q-32785" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3t-3 \\\\ y=7-9t \\\\ z=\\frac{3}{2}t-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3t-3 \\\\ 7-9t \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}t-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ -9t \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(-3,7,-\\frac{1}{2})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}].$"}]}
